{
  "0": "Learning objective: add 0.2 times mean softplus(s_neg - s_pos) to the original prediction loss over valid training positions, using exactly the existing sampled positive/negative pairs. This pairwise term may improve candidate ordering and validation HR@10 while retaining absolute-score supervision. Preserve sampling, scoring, SASRec architecture, optimizer and training schedule; train one model per category.",
  "1": "Interaction mechanism: replace dot-product compatibility with sum_d h_d * (1 + 0.5*tanh(a_d)) * e_item,d, where a is one jointly learned vector initialized to zero per category. Bounded dimension weights may suppress noisy compatibility dimensions while starting at baseline scoring. Preserve the causal backbone, input features, history readout, loss and optimizer. Update the predictor writer to load and apply the same single-model scorer.",
  "2": "Interest aggregation: replace each last-state readout with 0.8*h_t + 0.2*m_t, where m_t is the normalized exponential average of valid causal encoder states through t, with a five-interaction half-life. This may stabilize sparse histories while emphasizing current intent. Use prefix-only pooling at every supervised training position and the identical final-prefix readout at prediction. Preserve features, backbone, scoring, loss and optimizer.",
  "3": "Sequence modeling: halve the original maximum context length, rounding down with a minimum of one, and retain the most recent interactions in chronological order with baseline padding and positional-index conventions. A shorter causal context may reduce stale-interest noise and improve HR@10 after the previous context-expansion direction underperformed. Apply the same truncation in training and the generated predictor; preserve embedding design, backbone, readout, loss and optimizer."
}
